From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:37:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Add TpSetWaitEx, and return from TpSetTimerEx whether
 the timer was still to go off.

Office's AI component (aitrx.dll and ai.dll) imports the Ex functions of
the thread pool.  Upstream has since added TpSetTimerEx, which returns
whether the timer was set; Windows 11 build 29671 returns whether it
was still to go off: a one-shot timer that went off stays set, as
TpIsTimerSet says, but gives FALSE, and a periodic one TRUE.  TpSetWaitEx
sets the wait like TpSetWait and returns the same of the wait: one
satisfied by its object gives FALSE.  The tests pass there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

